f different things that  make life richer and I guess an example  my favorite example that I love to think  of is when it rains and you know the the  water stops and the Sun comes out and  there's a beautiful rainbow in the sky I  think we often forget how amazing  rainbows are because they're just part  of reality so we're like well that's  normal why wouldn't it be but when you  think about it like if you were to tell  someone hey by the way after the rain  this is crazy  perfectly circular spectrum of colors  that's just sitting in the middle of the  air as if by magic that's a crazy idea  now my question and where mathematics  comes into this is why why is that there  and why is a rainbow perfectly round I  mean it's a semicircle if you look at it  from the ground but if you're up in the  air if you're lucky enough to be in a  plane when it happened you'll see it is  a perfect circle why is that how is it  that a million raindrops are conspiring  together to create this object of  immense beauty in the air and there's a  wonderful little piece of circle  geometry that tells us why now do you  need to know that well you don't need to  but when you do you can appreciate the  world in a much deeper and richer way  and I love that mathematics gives us  access to that Eddy whoo you are  conquering the seeds of math for me this  afternoon you are making it something  that I might even be able to justify to  with my old brain everyone can  everything from fixed to fluid I think  is the way you were talking about it  Blatter oh and it is certainly fodder  for the future this evening channeling  mr. woo it premieres on Australian story  eight o'clock this evening with Eddie  whoo it will make you want to get back  into math or at least think about it a  little bit more Eddie thank you so much  for sharing can't wait to see your story  tonight it's a great pleasure thanks  your time
 

